{
  "_comment": "What counts as a command that only reads (scripts\\lib\\CommandRules.ps1, docs\\security.md): such commands run in every mode without a question. A command line counts only when every part of it is understood and every option is listed here; everything else asks, so a missing option costs a question and never lets something through. The names must also stand in readOnlyCommands or readOnlyGit of config\\unzensiert.json, where you take commands out. bash: short = allowed one-letter options (also together, -la), long = allowed long options without the dashes (a value may follow after =), operands = at most this many words that are no options, plus = words may start with + (date). find: the allowed tests. git: long options per subcommand; gitShort: one-letter options (default for all others). powershell: parameters per cmdlet (may be abbreviated), aliases: names that mean a cmdlet, blocks: cmdlets that may take a { } which only compares values. recursive: commands that walk through folders; they ask when a protected folder (secretPaths in config\\guard.json) lies below. After a change run scripts\\Test-Security.ps1.",

